{"context_ids": [], "controls": [{"control_id": "sota004", "description": "SOTA #4 with the contiguous 4-gram (NGRAM_FOURGRAM_SPAN=3), same seed & data order.", "kind": "no_intervention", "matching": {"same_checkpoint": true, "same_data_order": true}}], "created_at": "2026-07-23T02:50:00-07:00", "estimated_cost": {"basis": "6 concurrent 2000-step H200 runs", "cost_tier": "light", "currency_cost": 0.0, "gpu_hours": 2.2}, "expected_effect": {"direction": "increase", "estimand": "endpoint_val_bpb_delta_vs_sota004", "latency_steps": 0}, "falsification": {"decision_rule": "Three-way read on the 3-seed paired delta. delta in [0, +0.0008] -> SPARSITY-MEDIATED (supports the dose-response model). delta >= +0.0012 -> RANGE DECAY / adjacency-specific information. delta <= 0 -> reach beats recency; escalate the gappy shape as a SOTA candidate to 6 hold-out seeds.", "failure_condition": "An intermediate delta near +0.0004 supports sparsity mediation and CONFIRMS the order ceiling is a data-budget artifact, not an architectural limit.", "minimum_seeds": 3}, "fingerprint": "609f2571d2afc7b2", "hypothesis_id": "hyp_gappy_fourgram_sparsity_dose", "intervention": {"intervention_id": "int_sota004_gappy4", "parameters": {"env": {"DOC_MASK": "1", "DOC_MASK_MODE": "seg", "NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT": "256", "NGRAM_FOURGRAM_SPAN": "4", "NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD": "1", "NGRAM_STATE_ROWWISE": "1", "NGRAM_TABLE_MULT": "256", "WARMDOWN_RATIO": "0.75"}}, "version": 1}, "mechanism_ids": ["mech_ngram_short_context_memory"], "notes": "Follows evd_obs_ngram_context_repeat_rate, which supplied the singleton rates AND refuted this probe's original 'sparsity-matched' framing before any GPU time was spent. Costs zero extra VRAM.", "observable_predictions": [], "outcome": {"outcome_id": "out_val_bpb", "version": 1}, "prediction": "The order ladder stops at 4-gram. Two rival causes: (a) SPARSITY -- longer contexts recur too rarely at 294.9M tokens for a hashed row to accumulate gradient; (b) RANGE DECAY -- distant tokens simply carry little marginal information. The gappy 4-gram (w[-4],w[-2],w[-1],w[0]) has a MEASURED singleton rate of 0.6030, between the contiguous 4-gram's 0.4576 and the 5-gram's 0.6992, so it is an intermediate dose on the sparsity axis while REACHING to position -4. QUANTITATIVE PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION: if singleton rate is the mediator, the gappy rung's value should interpolate between the measured 4-gram (-0.001206) and 5-gram (-0.000470) rung values on the same seeds, landing near -0.00076 -- i.e. the gappy arm should be WORSE than the contiguous control by only about +0.00044. If instead the gappy arm loses most of the 4-gram contribution (delta >= +0.0012, as bad as having no 4-gram at all), sparsity is NOT the whole story and the ADJACENT position w[-3] carries specific information that w[-4] cannot substitute for => RANGE DECAY. If the gappy arm is EQUAL OR BETTER than contiguous (delta <= 0), then reach beats recency and the contiguous window was the wrong shape all along.", "status": "proposed", "tags": ["ngram", "fourgram", "context_shape", "gappy", "dose_response", "explore"], "title": "Is the n-gram order ceiling caused by CONTEXT SPARSITY or by RANGE DECAY?", "trigger": {"condition": {"operator": "initial_loss_is_finite"}, "observable_id": "", "type": "run_start"}, "version": 1}
